// Stage E2 (f_tf_hatch v2): the streamline march. in1 = E1's aux (ca, sa, coh,
// pres), render-sized (Width / Height Params = its size). Mirrors
// tests/modules/tf_hatch/tf_hatch_mirror.py stage_e2 (sparse mode).
//
// Per pixel: march N = 16 steps each way along the local axis, accumulating
// sparse impulse noise. All geometry is in PIXEL units (steps are uniform in
// pixels, so a non-square frame still gets round streaks).
//   - sign continuity: the axis has no sign; each step flips it to agree with
//     the previous direction (dot product), so there is no branch cut.
//   - coherence enters ONLY as persistence (spec OQ1): d = normalize(w*a +
//     (1-w)*r), w = coh^0.5, r = a per-pixel/per-step hashed unit vector.
//     Coherent regions march ballistically (streaks), incoherent ones random-
//     walk (grain). Never shape, never brightness.
//   - noise lives in WORLD coordinates: round BLOB impulses from rotated value
//     noise (blob_noise below; lattice scale from `grain`), thresholded so their
//     coverage equals the lit probability set by `density`.
//   - brightness = blob coverage crossed (acc * step / cell_px), so one
//     impulse's stroke has brightness ~1 whatever reach and grain are (a low-
//     density blob peaks below 1: same expected coverage, dimmer peak).
//   - a path that leaves the frame stops contributing (`alive` latch).
//   - the step must not exceed the cell size (step <= cell_px) or cells can be
//     skipped; at N = 16 this bounds reach against grain.
//
// Coordinates: `norm` = (i + 0.5)/size (texel centres; tests/lib/gpu_sim.py,
// jxf.py), so the pixel's own texel centre is norm*size = i + 0.5. (`cell`
// would be norm*(size-1): not used.) Reads: `nearest` at (pos/size). size = the
// Width / Height Params (never `dim`: see below).
//
// Params (names avoid GenExpr operators: `length` is one, hence `reach`):
//   reach    0..1  half-length of the march = reach * 0.25 * frame height
//   grain    0..1  noise cell size, log: cells per frame height =
//                  2^((1-grain)*6+3)
//   density  0..1  impulse coverage = 0.0025 * 2^(5*density), via the
//                  closed-form blob threshold
//   coh_floor   0..1  stroke termination (below): 0 = off
//   src_stroke  internal: 1 when the optional stroke-texture inlet (in2) is connected
// out1 = (raw blob-coverage-crossed, pres, 0, 1)   (texture connected: raw = the mean impulse along the path)
//
// COHERENCE FLOOR (2026-10-29; mirror: coh_floor; Matt's choice, "Terminate", from the Clouds / Dark / Terminate
// sheet; this supersedes spec OQ1's "coherence only as persistence" for coh_floor > 0). Each step's contribution is
// scaled by smoothstep(coh_floor - 0.2, coh_floor, coherence at the step's start): strokes end where direction is
// lost, and the pixel's own presence (what E3 multiplies by) is scaled by the same ramp on its OWN coherence, so an
// undirected region goes BLACK (Matt, 2026-10-29: keeping the pixel's own mark read as bright dots, not black). At 0
// both factors are exactly 1, so the default is today's look bit for bit. One smoothstep and one multiply per step.
//
// STROKE TEXTURE (2026-10-29; mirror: texture_coord / texture_impulse): with in2 connected the impulse is
// the texture's Rec.709 luma, soft-thresholded, instead of a blob; the marks are then the texture streaked
// along the contours. Grain = ZOOM: the texture is tiled 2^((1-grain)*6) times across the frame (grain 1 =
// once, 64 tiles at grain 0; same six octaves as the blob cell). Density = the soft threshold on the luma:
// smoothstep(thr - 0.1, thr + 0.1, luma), thr = 1.1 - 1.2 * density. Sampled by `nearest` at the
// frame-normalized march position. Brightness = acc / wsum, the plain LIC mean (not blob coverage crossed).
// COST (bench, 1080p, E2 alone; the module adds ~1.5 ms for E1 + E3): blobs 3.0 ms. Texture mode is memory-bound, not
// arithmetic-bound (a 4x4 texture costs 2.7): the texture's size times the tiling stride. A float32 1080p texture
// costs 13 ms at Grain 0.5 and 12.5 at Grain 0 but 5.0 at Grain 1 (read once, sequential); 256x256 4.8, 512x512 5.1,
// 1024x1024 6.9 at Grain 0.5. Fetch count and the if/else cost nothing (probes 1 and 2). Since 2026-10-30 in2 is
// NOT the raw inlet texture: the pre-stage (codebox_stage_pre_h / _pre_v) box-filters it to render size / 4 on each
// axis first, so E2 reads a 480x270 texture at 1080p: 5.0 ms (bench), module about 7.4 ms in texture mode.

// Hashes WITHOUT sin (Hoskins' "hash without sine"): sin(ix*127.1+iy*311.7)*43758
// loses all precision on the GPU once the argument reaches ~1e4-1e5 (1080p
// lattices), which can make the lit-cell pattern clump and flip with tiny
// `grain` changes. Every intermediate here stays below ~1e3.
hash12(ha, hb) {
    hx = fract(ha * 0.1031);
    hy = fract(hb * 0.1031);
    hz = hx;
    hd = hx * (hy + 33.33) + hy * (hz + 33.33) + hz * (hx + 33.33);
    hx = hx + hd;
    hy = hy + hd;
    hz = hz + hd;
    return fract((hx + hy) * hz);
}

hash13(ha, hb, hc) {
    hx = fract(ha * 0.1031);
    hy = fract(hb * 0.1031);
    hz = fract(hc * 0.1031);
    hd = hx * (hz + 31.32) + hy * (hy + 31.32) + hz * (hx + 31.32);
    hx = hx + hd;
    hy = hy + hd;
    hz = hz + hd;
    return fract((hx + hy) * hz);
}

// Band-limited blob impulse (2026-10-29; mirror: blob_noise / value_noise). Quintic value
// noise on a lattice ROTATED 22.5 deg (cos 0.9238795, sin 0.3826834: the pixel's axis and
// diagonal directions see the same noise), thresholded with a soft ramp. Replaces the lit
// lattice cells, whose squares painted axis-aligned rectangles. bext = (W + H)/cell keeps
// the lattice index positive after the rotation. Four hash12 taps per sample.
blob_noise(cx, cy, cell_sz, bthr, bwid, bext) {
    bu = (0.9238795 * cx - 0.3826834 * cy) / cell_sz + bext;
    bv = (0.3826834 * cx + 0.9238795 * cy) / cell_sz + bext;
    bi = floor(bu);
    bj = floor(bv);
    bfu = bu - bi;
    bfv = bv - bj;
    bfu = bfu * bfu * bfu * (bfu * (bfu * 6.0 - 15.0) + 10.0);
    bfv = bfv * bfv * bfv * (bfv * (bfv * 6.0 - 15.0) + 10.0);
    bh00 = hash12(bi, bj);
    bh10 = hash12(bi + 1.0, bj);
    bh01 = hash12(bi, bj + 1.0);
    bh11 = hash12(bi + 1.0, bj + 1.0);
    bn = (bh00 * (1.0 - bfu) + bh10 * bfu) * (1.0 - bfv) + (bh01 * (1.0 - bfu) + bh11 * bfu) * bfv;
    return smoothstep(bthr - bwid, bthr + bwid, bn);
}

Param reach(0.5);
Param grain(0.5);
Param density(0.7);
Param src_stroke(0.0);    // 1 when the stroke-texture inlet is connected (vs_inState)
Param coh_floor(0.0);     // 0..1: a stroke ends where the coherence along its path drops (0 = off)
// Render size. NOT `dim`: live jit.gl.pix cannot read its own size (`dim` reads ~1 x 1 in a
// Vsynth chain, found 2026-10-29: with dim ~ 1 the position clamp [0.5, dim - 0.5] pins every
// march step to the frame centre, so nothing follows the tensor). Vsynth drives these two Params
// (definition `render_dim`: `r dim` -> `prepend param width/height`); nobody sets them by hand.
Param width(1920.0);
Param height(1080.0);

wpx = width;
hpx = height;
x0 = norm.x * wpx;
y0 = norm.y * hpx;

half_len = reach * 0.25 * hpx;
h_step = half_len / 16.0;
cell_px = hpx / pow(2.0, (1.0 - grain) * 6.0 + 3.0);
// blob threshold: a closed-form cubic in density, fit so the soft-ramped coverage equals the
// lit probability 0.0025 * 2^(5 density) (mirror BLOB_THR; blob_fit.py; worst error 3.2%)
blob_thr = 0.999341 + density * (-0.092880 + density * (0.011592 + density * -0.084665));
blob_wid = 0.079065;                  // 0.35 * 0.2259 (BLOB_SOFT * BLOB_STD)
blob_ext = (wpx + hpx) / cell_px;
persist_pow = 0.5;
tex_on = step(0.5, src_stroke);
tiles = pow(2.0, (1.0 - grain) * 6.0);
tex_thr = 1.1 - 1.2 * density;

ca0 = nearest(in1, norm).x;
sa0 = nearest(in1, norm).y;
pres0 = nearest(in1, norm).w;
coh0 = nearest(in1, norm).z;     // this pixel's own coherence (the Coh Floor black-out)
// unset axis (0, 0) -> a fixed fallback axis (E3 multiplies by presence 0 there)
m0 = sqrt(ca0 * ca0 + sa0 * sa0);
ok0 = step(0.000001, m0);
ca0 = mix(1.0, ca0 / max(m0, 0.000001), ok0);
sa0 = mix(0.0, sa0 / max(m0, 0.000001), ok0);

imp = 0.0;
if (tex_on > 0.5) {
    tu = fract(tiles * x0 / wpx);
    tv = fract(tiles * y0 / hpx);
    tl = 0.2126 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).x + 0.7152 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).y + 0.0722 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).z;
    imp = smoothstep(tex_thr - 0.1, tex_thr + 0.1, tl);
} else {
    imp = blob_noise(x0, y0, cell_px, blob_thr, blob_wid, blob_ext);
}
acc = imp;
wsum = 1.0;
px = x0;
py = y0;
dx = 0.0;
dy = 0.0;
alive = 1.0;
sgn = 1.0;
for (side = 0; side < 2; side += 1) {
    px = x0;
    py = y0;
    alive = 1.0;
    sgn = 1.0 - 2.0 * side;
    dx = sgn * ca0;
    dy = sgn * sa0;
    for (k = 1; k <= 16; k += 1) {
        ux = px / wpx;      // px is clamped to [0.5, W-0.5]: strictly inside (0, 1)
        uy = py / hpx;
        ax = nearest(in1, vec(ux, uy)).x;
        ay = nearest(in1, vec(ux, uy)).y;
        coh = nearest(in1, vec(ux, uy)).z;
        am = sqrt(ax * ax + ay * ay);
        oka = step(0.000001, am);
        ax = mix(1.0, ax / max(am, 0.000001), oka);
        ay = mix(0.0, ay / max(am, 0.000001), oka);
        dp = ax * dx + ay * dy;
        flipv = 2.0 * step(0.0, dp) - 1.0;
        ax = ax * flipv;
        ay = ay * flipv;
        wgt = pow(clamp(coh, 0.0, 1.0), persist_pow);
        ang = twopi * hash13(floor(x0), floor(y0), k + 32.0 * side);
        mx = wgt * ax + (1.0 - wgt) * cos(ang);
        my = wgt * ay + (1.0 - wgt) * sin(ang);
        mm = sqrt(mx * mx + my * my);
        okm = step(0.000001, mm);
        ax = mix(ax, mx / max(mm, 0.000001), okm);
        ay = mix(ay, my / max(mm, 0.000001), okm);
        nx = px + h_step * ax;
        ny = py + h_step * ay;
        alive = alive * step(0.0, nx) * step(nx, wpx) * step(0.0, ny) * step(ny, hpx);
        alive = alive * smoothstep(coh_floor - 0.2, coh_floor, coh);   // 1 exactly at coh_floor 0
        px = clamp(nx, 0.5, wpx - 0.5);
        py = clamp(ny, 0.5, hpx - 0.5);
        dx = ax;
        dy = ay;
        if (tex_on > 0.5) {
            tu = fract(tiles * px / wpx);
            tv = fract(tiles * py / hpx);
            tl = 0.2126 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).x + 0.7152 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).y + 0.0722 * nearest(in2, vec(tu, tv)).z;
            imp = smoothstep(tex_thr - 0.1, tex_thr + 0.1, tl);
        } else {
            imp = blob_noise(px, py, cell_px, blob_thr, blob_wid, blob_ext);
        }
        acc = acc + alive * imp;
        wsum = wsum + alive;
    }
}
raw = mix(acc * h_step / cell_px, acc / wsum, tex_on);
out1 = vec(raw, pres0 * smoothstep(coh_floor - 0.2, coh_floor, coh0), 0.0, 1.0);   // 1 exactly at coh_floor 0
